id: examples/node
title: "examples node"
kind: mental-model-node
status: active-mixed
updated: 2026-08-27

purpose: >
  Hold small example yawns so a person can see the protocol in ordinary use.

holds:
  - stuck example
  - decision example
  - yawn spine dogfood example
  - relationship tension example
  - relationship commitment conversation example
  - signal example
  - choice example
  - repair example
  - context-free agent cold-start fixture
  - state-substrate family example
  - nested agent-arena holarchy example
  - asynchronous waiting and resume example
  - conversation import routing example
  - merge versus link versus split example
  - Dave / good dad objective holon and Yawn.bot example
  - sanitized participation-choice orientation example

receives:
  - templates
  - common lived situations
  - proof and boundary rules
  - state, desire, optional target, authority, and event-reduction contracts

produces:
  - concrete starting points
  - readable demonstrations
  - copyable patterns

questions:
  - what does a simple yawn look like
  - how does proof appear in an example
  - what boundary keeps the example safe

links:
  - templates/node.yawn
  - questions/node.yawn
  - start/first-yawn.yawn
